// torven_core.udl — Torven Core FFI surface declaration.
//
// This file declares every Rust function, type, enum, and callback interface
// that crosses the Swift <-> Rust FFI boundary. Generated by UniFFI 0.27 at
// build time (see `build.rs`). The Swift bindings are produced by
// `uniffi-bindgen generate --language swift` and consumed by the SwiftUI app
// in `apple/Torven/`.
//
// Architecture reference: docs/architecture/torven-v1-adr.md#adr-4
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Type conventions (MUST follow across every function added to this UDL):
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// * Primitives:  string, i32, i64, f64, boolean
// * Timestamps:  always i64 representing Unix epoch milliseconds.
//                Convert to Date on the Swift side and to DateTime<Utc> on
//                the Rust side. Never expose chrono types directly.
// * Monetary:    always f64 representing US dollars. Vendors return USD;
//                if a future vendor returns a different currency, normalize
//                in Rust before crossing FFI.
// * Optional:    `T?` (nullable). Maps to Swift `T?` and Rust `Option<T>`.
// * Lists:       `sequence<T>`. Prefer batched/paginated APIs (e.g.
//                `list_snapshots(limit: i32)`) over `get_all_*` to avoid
//                large allocations crossing FFI (see AR-3 in ADR).
// * Errors:      define a UDL `enum` of error variants and tag the function
//                with `[Throws=ErrorType]`. Maps to Swift `throws` and Rust
//                `Result<T, ErrorType>`.
// * Strings:     always UTF-8. See SECURITY note below.
// * Async:       use `[Async]` annotation (UniFFI 0.25+) when the Rust impl
//                is `async fn`. Required for streaming endpoints
//                (Story 1.15 — AI Insights).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECURITY (NON-NEGOTIABLE):
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// NEVER expose `api_key`, OAuth tokens, refresh tokens, or any user secret
// through this FFI surface as a `string`. Secrets MUST be persisted via the
// Keychain helpers (`keychain_get_blob` / `keychain_set_blob` — added in a
// later story) and referenced by opaque vendor + account IDs in the FFI.
// Strings crossing FFI are eligible to appear in crash logs, telemetry, and
// developer dumps.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

namespace torven_core {
    // Smoke-test function — validates that the Rust -> FFI -> Swift pipeline
    // is wired correctly end-to-end before any real business surface is
    // added. Returns the constant string "pong".
    //
    // This is the AR-1 spike validation function (see Story 1.2). It will be
    // kept long-term as a no-op health check that the SwiftUI app can call on
    // launch to confirm the bundled XCFramework loaded successfully.
    string ping();
};
